                                        "entry_id": "4a58ef10-6d14-37b8-97e6-ea11a8a6456a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lexeme that consists of more than one stem or an affix, e.g. \\\"bookshop\\\", \\\"high school\\\" or \\\"non-standard\\\"."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e7d81d8-b806-49de-8c34-036446af3677",
                                                "sense_id": "156ec503-4fae-3302-a795-f6d033b3e523",
                                                "text": "In the majority of the compounds of non- the hyphen is usually retained; but it is commonly omitted in the case of a few, such as nonconformist, nonentity, nonsense, in which the etymology has been to some extent lost sight of."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fec22cac-cde1-3850-aaf4-af768cb1b5a5",
                                        "entry_id": "4a58ef10-6d14-37b8-97e6-ea11a8a6456a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A compound locomotive, a steam locomotive with both high-pressure and low-pressure cylinders."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8f8d56b-67d6-4ee0-97a6-29fda58aa661",
                                                "sense_id": "fec22cac-cde1-3850-aaf4-af768cb1b5a5",
                                                "text": "From a dead stand, with regulator full open and the lever at about 50 per cent we got up to about 60 m.p.h. by the top of the bank. The big compound was making plenty of noise - but what musical and wonderful noise!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fce8f0fe-48d4-357e-9861-756184bcc217",
                                        "entry_id": "4a58ef10-6d14-37b8-97e6-ea11a8a6456a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of compound exercise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "compound",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "303be380-77ba-370f-a713-2a5e2107cbf8",
                                        "entry_id": "04f71598-8dd9-3ef8-a09d-ca12ed838911",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To form (a resulting mixture) by combining different elements, ingredients, or parts; to mingle with something else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2b17370-6a7c-464a-8404-34b615407107",
                                                "sense_id": "303be380-77ba-370f-a713-2a5e2107cbf8",
                                                "text": "to compound a medicine"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "026526e9-8e39-4cfe-a9ad-c4083f92625f",
                                                "sense_id": "303be380-77ba-370f-a713-2a5e2107cbf8",
                                                "text": "Only compound me with forgotten dust."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efecf7b4-71f4-4a69-b80c-710b5fb99c2c",
                                                "sense_id": "303be380-77ba-370f-a713-2a5e2107cbf8",
                                                "text": "We have the power of altering[…] and compounding those images[…] into all the varieties of picture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2f8172d-c360-4ec3-8818-b03d24a8202b",
                                                "sense_id": "303be380-77ba-370f-a713-2a5e2107cbf8",
                                                "text": "incapacitating him from successfully compounding a tale of this sort"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5cfde22-3462-442c-aa24-b8a13cb2cb8b",
                                                "sense_id": "303be380-77ba-370f-a713-2a5e2107cbf8",
                                                "text": "In eighteenth century France, many aphrodisiac dishes and pastries were compounded with chocolate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6d5ae3f3-69a2-3ece-866c-7fd86f3d7420",
                                        "entry_id": "04f71598-8dd9-3ef8-a09d-ca12ed838911",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To settle by agreeing on less than the claim, or on different terms than those stipulated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "412d8b39-8e22-48e2-895a-70af4faab166",
                                                "sense_id": "6d5ae3f3-69a2-3ece-866c-7fd86f3d7420",
                                                "text": "to compound a debt"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d79f13a-78b5-32ea-b933-cbef7c19474c",
                                        "entry_id": "04f71598-8dd9-3ef8-a09d-ca12ed838911",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To settle amicably; to adjust by agreement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebc52bf0-e4a1-4e43-9cdd-18f0ae47bb43",
                                                "sense_id": "8d79f13a-78b5-32ea-b933-cbef7c19474c",
                                                "text": "I pray, my lords, let me compound this strife."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bb2ba17-46f2-4671-ae91-02135ec5770b",
                                                "sense_id": "8d79f13a-78b5-32ea-b933-cbef7c19474c",
                                                "text": "No! no—if Charles has done nothing false or mean, I shall compound for his extravagance"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7b7f5d4-5d34-3b85-bbf0-c3dc295b90e0",
                                        "entry_id": "04f71598-8dd9-3ef8-a09d-ca12ed838911",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To come to terms of agreement; to settle by a compromise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b17498ab-226c-4f7c-87ae-f5fb94661b04",
                                                "sense_id": "d7b7f5d4-5d34-3b85-bbf0-c3dc295b90e0",
                                                "text": "to compound with someone / for something"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5dc2a3c0-369b-4c95-8ba5-923196db5fe7",
                                                "sense_id": "d7b7f5d4-5d34-3b85-bbf0-c3dc295b90e0",
                                                "text": "Here's a fellow will help you to-morrow; […] compound with him by the year."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a527f15-e99a-4289-a642-5ec7f3bfe9ab",
                                                "sense_id": "d7b7f5d4-5d34-3b85-bbf0-c3dc295b90e0",
                                                "text": "They were at last glad to compound for his bare commitment to the Tower."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2178dc5-93da-46dd-b406-9bc86d513390",
                                                "sense_id": "d7b7f5d4-5d34-3b85-bbf0-c3dc295b90e0",
                                                "text": "[Cornwall] compounded to furnish ten oxen after Michaelmas for thirty pounds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b969cb1-5cbb-42be-8d1c-6b4f8869352a",
                                                "sense_id": "d7b7f5d4-5d34-3b85-bbf0-c3dc295b90e0",
                                                "text": "Compound for sins they are inclined to / By damning those they have no mind to."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9923ba03-a0e3-37b0-a01e-85f9cb5c7622",
                                        "entry_id": "04f71598-8dd9-3ef8-a09d-ca12ed838911",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To compose; to constitute."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feddbef3-a132-41c6-b22a-f4350306e362",
                                                "sense_id": "9923ba03-a0e3-37b0-a01e-85f9cb5c7622",
                                                "text": "his pomp and all what state compounds"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b2434e8e-127f-3c33-9e4b-5d597cc2e6d1",
                                        "entry_id": "04f71598-8dd9-3ef8-a09d-ca12ed838911",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To increase in value with interest, where the interest is earned on both the principal sum and prior earned interest."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "103a0812-54b4-307e-9b86-8b7e7ad25fa1",
                                        "entry_id": "04f71598-8dd9-3ef8-a09d-ca12ed838911",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To worsen a situation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "968b2150-44dd-49f3-befd-241b6388cb15",
                                                "sense_id": "103a0812-54b4-307e-9b86-8b7e7ad25fa1",
                                                "text": "[…] This latest example of nationalistic self-interest compounded anger across the EU over Trump’s travel ban, imposed last month without consultation or scientific justification."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "903d26fc-a9a2-391c-a1ac-3d5b9352e79d",
                                        "entry_id": "04f71598-8dd9-3ef8-a09d-ca12ed838911",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a horse: to fail to maintain speed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4638007-2ce6-4536-98ad-0f6dc9f2993f",
                                                "sense_id": "903d26fc-a9a2-391c-a1ac-3d5b9352e79d",
                                                "text": "At the hill, the Warrior must have been at least ten lengths in front of Wild Dayrell; but he compounded about 200 yards on the T. Y. C. side of the Red House."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
